      "text": [
        " خَبَرٍ آخَرَ : سُئِلَ أَبُو جَعْفَرٍ عَلَيْهِ اَلسَّلاَمُ عَنْ قَوْلِ اَللَّهِ عَزَّ وَ جَلَّ \"وَ لاٰ تُؤْتُوا اَلسُّفَهٰاءَ أَمْوٰالَكُمُ\" قَالَ \"لاَ تُؤْتُوهَا شَارِبَ اَلْخَمْرِ وَ لاَ اَلنِّسَاءَ\" ثُمَّ قَالَ \"وَ أَيُّ سَفِيهٍ أَسْفَهُ مِنْ شَارِبِ اَلْخَمْرِ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.5534 - In another narration, Abu Jafar Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as), was asked about the saying of Allah (swt), the Almighty and Glorious:\n\"And do not give the weak-minded your wealth.\" (Qur'an 4:5).\nImam (as) said: \"Do not give it to one who drinks alcohol or to women.\"\nThen Imam (as) added: \"And who is more foolish than a person who drinks alcohol?\""
        ]
      }
